{
 "meta": {
  "about": "Hand-checked High level / Budget gear, applied over bosses.json when the site loads (bosses.json is regenerated from the Wiki guides by scripts, this file is not). A gear entry is an item key, or a list of keys that count as equal (owning any one covers the slot; if none are owned it's priced at the first). dropSupplies removes guide supply lines that don't fit the setup. noGear marks a setup that needs no gear (always affordable). bosses.<id>.taskOnly marks a boss that can only be fought on a Slayer task: it isn't used for planner 'make GP' steps. An entry can also be { item, qty }: ammo is always 200 (players rarely hold less), counted as gear to own; what's fired per kill stays in supplies. set overrides setup fields such as unitsPerHr and lootShare. copyOf creates a setup (e.g. Budget) from another one of the same boss, then applies gear/set/dropSupplies.",
  "rules": "Strategy page Equipment table, best (left) column. Follow footnotes where a cell has '/', otherwise take the cheaper item. Drop items made redundant by a 2h weapon; keep the special attack row. Content needing several styles combines the tables (ToB: all melee, all ranged, 5 magic pieces)."
 },
